                                "sense_id": "f7418f53-a9d3-331e-91ef-dbd171a63420",
                                "text": "On th' other side in all mens open vew Duessa placed is, and on a tree Sans-foy his[*] shield is hangd with bloody hew: Both those[*] the lawrell girlonds to the victor dew. 45 VI A shrilling trompet sownded from on hye, And unto battaill bad them selves addresse: Their shining shieldes about their wrestes they tye, And burning blades about their heads do blesse, The instruments of wrath and heavinesse: 50 With greedy force each other doth assayle, And strike so fiercely, that they do impresse Deepe dinted furrowes in the battred mayle; The yron walles to ward their blowes are weak and fraile.",
                                "translation": "另一边站着男士们，两眼大张，无信无念的血染盾牌铮铮亮，杜艾莎将它高挂在一棵树上：胜利的月桂花冠已准备妥当。一阵刺耳的喇叭声响彻天边，他们二人双双分别高喊开展，护在手腕的两块盾牌亮闪闪，举在头顶的是明晃晃的利剑，这些愤怒的武器都重如泰山，贪婪的威力在彼此身上试验，疯狂的戳刺留下刀痕一串串，在彼此铠甲上化下沟沟坎坎，道道铁墙防御，攻击弱不堪言。（邢怡译）"
                            },
                            {
